    "collapsible_content_TUC6pH": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_GW8rJj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do your filters work?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We use the highest grade 304 stainless steel, natural coconut carbon and other natural materials. Plus the mighty force of gravity! Our advanced filtration system removes up to 99.99% of commonly occurring contaminants and retains up to 100% of minerals. <a href=\"/pages/new-our-tech\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Our Tech\">Click here</a> for more information on how it works.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_7x6WWW": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What do your filters really remove?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Carbon filters are made from pure coconut shells, which are a sustainable and a renewable resource. The carbon in the filters are activated, which means that it has a high surface area and is very porous. This allows them to trap a wide range of contaminants, including chlorine, heavy metals, and other impurities. Phoenix Gravity Carbon cartridges are designed to provide clean, odorless water with a great taste. They do not release any harmful chemicals or by-products into the water, and they are super effective at removing chlorine and other volatile organic compounds A pair of carbon cartridges can filter up to 20,000 liters of water by providing safe and healthy drinking water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YqdXBf": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters remove residual pharmaceutical waste?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, up to 99.99%! Our primary Smart Carbon Cartridges have been independently tested for many Volatile Organic compounds including 1,4- dichlorobenzene, 2-Butanone, Acetone, Allyl Chloride and many more. For full test results, <a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\">click here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_BTFxHp": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do the Phoenix Carbon Cartridges remove fluoride?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>They certainly can! We’ve designed a specialist fluoride cartridge called the POSTreat to remove over 95% of fluoride from your tap water. Made from the highest grade stainless steel, it’s completely reusable and refillable, with our POSTreat FluoRid Refill. The POSTtreat can be used in conjunction with primary Carbon Cartridges. For full details or to buy the POSTreat, <a href=\"/products/postreat-fluoride-remover\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter Cartridge\">click here.</a> Looking for a refill? <a href=\"/products/postreat-fluorid-media-refill\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"POSTreat FluoRid Media Refill\">Click here</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_MbNLHd": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Carbon Cartridges eliminate phthalates from water?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of phthalates, our Phoenix Carbon Cartridges are made with highest grade activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing phthalates from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters. Find the full list of what we remove <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/pages/help-center\">here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_WPwjUH": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity filters remove Estrogen?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of estrogen, our Phoenix Carbon Filters are made with activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing estrogen from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters. Find the full list of what we remove<a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\"> here</a>. <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22123241/\">https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22123241/</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_ARRB7k": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do your Gravity Filters and cartridges compare to others?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We are one of the leaders in advanced Gravity Filtration. With over 40 years’ experience of manufacturing in-house, we have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and cartridges. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become a leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Un8MXb": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are your filters as comprehensive as Berkey?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely! We have run extensive and independent tests on our filters for a variety of microbiological contaminants such as e-coli bacteria, MS2 Phage viruses and chemical contaminants such as Lead, chlorine, chromium, Volatile organic compounds and 100 more. What’s more, with over 40 years’ experience of in-house manufacturing - we’re one of the leading global manufacturers of stainless steel gravity filtration systems. We also have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and cartridges. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become the world’s leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters. For more details, <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/\">click here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_qcnCFw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters lower the TDS?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>TDS stands for Total Dissolved Solids and is measured in parts per million (ppm) or parts per billion (ppb). It’s a measure of the water’s organic and inorganic content including minerals. Natural water will have a TDS reading from minerals picked up from the rocks and ground it flows through. It’s generally accepted that 300 ppm is a good mineral content. We purposely do not bring our TDS to zero, because we’re all about preserving the minerals your body needs.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_b6mKGe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will Phoenix Gravity Filters remove water hardness?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. Phoenix Carbon Filter Cartridges are designed to remove up to 99.99% of bacteria, viruses, chlorine, lead and over 100 other unwanted substances from your drinking water. However, it’s important to note Phoenix Gravity Water Filters are not designed to lower water hardness. In fact, many of the natural minerals that make the water hard are essential to good health- we want to retain as many as possible! Hardness (and TDS) is measured in ppm, it’s generally accepted that 300 ppm is a good mineral content of water.<a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\"> Click here</a> for more details on what we remove.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
